            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Is it possible now to add a slash to directories? Unfortunately I'm using macOS terminal right now, and icons from mini.icons do not work, so the only way to distinguish directories and files is by its color.\r\n\r\nCould you please elaborate on \"icons from mini.icons do not work\"? If there is a font that doesn't support Nerd Font glyphs, then there are couple of options here:\r\n\r\n- Set up 'mini.icons' with [`config.style = 'ascii'`](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-icons.html#miniicons.config-style). This will not use Nerd Font glyphs for icons.\r\n- Customize a directory icon for 'mini.files' specifically, as [described in this example](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-files.html#minifiles-examples-customizeicons).",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is it possible now to add a slash to directories? Unfortunately I'm using macOS terminal right now, and icons from mini.icons do not work, so the only way to distinguish directories and files is by its color.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Could you please elaborate on \"icons from mini.icons do not work\"? If there is a font that doesn't support Nerd Font glyphs, then there are couple of options here:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Set up 'mini.icons' with <a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-icons.html#miniicons.config-style\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">config.style = 'ascii'</code></a>. This will not use Nerd Font glyphs for icons.</li>\n<li>Customize a directory icon for 'mini.files' specifically, as <a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-files.html#minifiles-examples-customizeicons\" rel=\"nofollow\">described in this example</a>.</li>\n</ul>",
            "bodyText": "Is it possible now to add a slash to directories? Unfortunately I'm using macOS terminal right now, and icons from mini.icons do not work, so the only way to distinguish directories and files is by its color.\n\nCould you please elaborate on \"icons from mini.icons do not work\"? If there is a font that doesn't support Nerd Font glyphs, then there are couple of options here:\n\nSet up 'mini.icons' with config.style = 'ascii'. This will not use Nerd Font glyphs for icons.\nCustomize a directory icon for 'mini.files' specifically, as described in this example.",
