                    "body": "Your comment made me realize that I've not installed any nerd font in this Mac; I'm so used to my Linux machine that I completely forgot about that.\r\n\r\nBut about my original comment, since I didn't get icons on mini.files, I was asking if it was possible to show a `/` after each directory, much like `ls` already does.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"521\" height=\"129\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 4 52 50 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f52b9102-4e3c-425a-9b55-ec38a6af44b2\" />\r\n\r\nThis is with broken icons\r\n\r\n<img width=\"779\" height=\"267\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 4 39 03 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2af21bdf-8a58-449c-85bc-f0255304e578\" />\r\n\r\nThis is without icons.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"521\" height=\"293\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 4 50 34 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/594c6aa5-7e80-4501-86d0-7f73173555b1\" />",
